    "created_at": "2021-03-05T21:15:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-03T09:41:54Z",
    "body": "> So in general, there's not a lot of interest in adding features to browsers which allow you to do something that you can already do, except doing it without JavaScript. You've posted a lot of these, and I think we'll give them a few days to see if any other people are running into the same issues, but we'll probably close them soon.\r\n\r\nBefore the date input was included and browsers put a widget on it, it could already be done with Javascript. A lot of things now can be done with HTML5 and CSS used to be done with Javascript. Even so, all those things have been added in HTML5 and CSS because doing them with HTML5 and CSS in a declarative way and having them in the browser is easier and less prone to errors.\r\n\r\n",
